Community Trust Bank is filing this SAR on customer Rebecca Lawson regarding suspected structuring of cash deposits. Lawson maintains personal checking account 77120489, opened on February 6, 2026. At account opening, Lawson identified herself as an administrative assistant earning approximately $62,000 annually and stated that she expected primarily payroll deposits and routine household expenses.

Between July 7, 2026, and August 14, 2026, Lawson made 11 cash deposits totaling $94,300. Individual deposits ranged from $7,500 to $9,800. On three occasions, Lawson made two cash deposits on the same day. Prior account activity showed minimal use of cash, with no cash deposit exceeding $1,200 during the preceding six months.

Within two business days of nine of the deposits, Lawson initiated outgoing electronic transfers totaling $81,600 to two external accounts held in the name of Lawson Consulting LLC. State corporate records show Lawson formed Lawson Consulting LLC on June 29, 2026 and is its sole registered member.

On August 8, 2026, bank personnel questioned Lawson regarding the source of an $8,900 cash deposit. Lawson stated that the funds represented consulting income. Review of her account and customer profile identified no prior indication that she operated a consulting business, and Lawson did not provide invoices, contracts, or other documentation supporting the stated source of funds.

Community Trust Bank considers the activity suspicious because Lawson conducted repeated cash deposits below $10,000, including multiple deposits on the same day, followed by rapid transfers to a recently established business account. The activity is inconsistent with Lawson’s stated occupation, anticipated account activity, and historical transaction profile and may indicate structuring intended to avoid currency transaction reporting requirements.

Community Trust Bank restricted electronic transfers from the account on August 15, 2026, pending further review. The account remains open as of the date of this filing. Account statements, deposit records, customer due diligence information, and supporting documentation are available upon request.
